From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:00:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/25] glm5next: support EAGLE3/DFlash aux hidden states
 through mHC

GLM-5.3-Flash (Glm5NextForCausalLM / Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration)
did not implement SupportsEagle3, so serving it with a DFlash drafter such
as incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 failed at startup with "Model does not
support EAGLE3 interface" (eagle3_utils.set_eagle3_aux_hidden_state_layers).

Declare SupportsEagle3 on both wrappers and make Glm5NextModel an
EagleModelMixin. The aux tensor cannot be the mixin's default
hidden_states + residual: under mHC (hc_mult=4) a non-final layer returns
(x, residual, post, comb) and defers its hc_post into the next layer's
fused post+pre kernel, so no plain hidden state exists at a layer
boundary. _aux_hidden_state() completes the deferred hc_post with a
dedicated MHCPostOp (a pure op; the layer loop keeps consuming the
original tuple) and contracts the streams with hc_contract, exactly like
the last mHC layer's epilogue. Non-mHC boundaries already carry the summed
stream. Aux id L is the stream entering layer L (eagle3_utils maps the
drafter's target_layer_ids [5, 14, 24, 33, 42] to [6, 15, 25, 34, 43]);
id end_layer is the final, already-contracted output. Captured states are
all-gathered and trimmed under sequence parallelism. forward returns
(hidden_states, aux_hidden_states) only when aux layers are captured.

Based on vllm-project/vllm#56983 by Shijin Zhang (@Dovis01), PR head
306f565407 (Apache-2.0); the model.py diff applies to v0.31.0 unchanged.
The CPU unit test is adapted from tests/models/glm5next/test_eagle3.py in
vllm-project/vllm#55423 by @zixi-qi (Apache-2.0), retargeted at #56983's
model-level _aux_post_op. The same hc_post + hc_contract capture is used
by #55682 (@Leoyzen), knapcio/GLM-5.3-Flash-4x-DGX-Spark-TP4
overlay/glm5next_model.py and the Kindling glm53_eagle3_aux patch; no code
was taken from those.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
